IMPORT prelude

-- Health Ombudsman Act 2013 (Queensland) -- what the other modules share: dates, business days, and the one
-- regulative vocabulary (the ombudsman's duties to decide and to tell the complainant, ss 35, 49, 50, 278).
--
-- SEAT: the person who makes a health service complaint (usually the person who received the health service, or a
-- parent, guardian or family member acting for them). See NOTES.md.
--
-- Dates: the prelude's built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY,
-- DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
--
-- "Business day" is not defined in this Act. It is the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) term, which is not deposited
-- and was not read; the reading taken (fork F1 in NOTES.md) is a day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public
-- holiday, with the public holidays supplied by the person as a list of dates. "Within n business days after" a day
-- ends at the end of the n-th business day after that day (the day itself not counted).
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Ombudsman Act 2013: shared dates and rules`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Dates`
-- ===================================================================================================================

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `first` `is on or before` `second` IF DATE_SERIAL `first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `second`

-- The number of days in month m of year y.
GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` `m` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_DAY (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`) MINUS 1))

-- "n months after" a day (n a whole number, 0 or more): the same day number n months on, or the last day of that month
-- where it is shorter (30 November plus 3 months is 28 or 29 February). "1 year" (s 85(1)) is 12 months on this
-- reading (fork F2).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`n` `months after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `months from January` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`months from January` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS ((`months from January` MINUS (`months from January` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the day number` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the days in month` `the new month` `the new year`
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day`
            ELSE `the days in month` `the new month` `the new year`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Business days (fork F1)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- 1 is Monday ... 5 is Friday, 6 is Saturday, 0 is Sunday (DATE_SERIAL of Monday 9 November 2026 is 1 modulo 7).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekday number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a business day` `the day` `the public holidays` IF
        `the weekday number of` `the day` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the weekday number of` `the day` AT MOST 5
    AND (NOT (elem (DATE_SERIAL `the day`) (map DATE_SERIAL `the public holidays`)))

-- The n-th business day after a day (the day itself not counted); n of 0 or less gives the day itself.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE, `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the business day after` `n` `the day` `the public holidays` MEANS
    IF `n` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `is a business day` `the next day` `the public holidays`
         THEN `the business day after` (`n` MINUS 1) `the next day` `the public holidays`
         ELSE `the business day after` `n` `the next day` `the public holidays`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS 1 `days after` `the day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `The regulative vocabulary (ss 35, 49, 50, 56, 278)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- The duties are the health ombudsman's; the seat meets them as "by when must this be done, and was I told in time".
DECLARE `Ombudsman party` IS ONE OF
    `the health ombudsman`

-- `decide on day` carries the day of the decision, counted in days from the start of the period, so that the notice
-- rule under HENCE can count its 5 business days from it.
DECLARE `Ombudsman act` IS ONE OF
    `decide on day` HAS `the decision offset` IS A NUMBER
    `give the complainant notice of the decision`

-- The calendar days the ombudsman has, from the decision, to give notice of it: to the end of the 5th business day
-- after the decision (s 278(1)); where the notice must also fall within the decision period (s 35(1)(b)), to the end
-- of that period if it is earlier.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the business days for the decision` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice must also be within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision offset days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the notice days allowed` `the start` `the public holidays` `the business days for the decision` `the notice must also be within the period` `the decision offset days` MEANS
    IF `the notice must also be within the period`
    THEN `the smaller of` `the s 278 days` `and` (`the number of days from` `the decision day` `until` `the period's last day`)
    ELSE `the s 278 days`
    WHERE
        `the decision day` MEANS `the decision offset days` `days after` `the start`
        `the s 278 days` MEANS `the number of days from` `the decision day` `until` (`the business day after` 5 `the decision day` `the public holidays`)
        `the period's last day` MEANS `the business day after` `the business days for the decision` `the start` `the public holidays`

-- THE RULE. s 35(1) "Within 7 business days after receiving a complaint, the health ombudsman must-- (a) decide ...;
-- and (b) give notice of the decision to the complainant ... under section 278." s 49(1) "The health ombudsman must
-- complete the assessment within 22 business days after deciding to carry out the assessment." s 50 "After completing
-- the assessment, the health ombudsman must-- (a) decide ...; and (b) give notice of the decision ... under section
-- 278." s 278(1) "As soon as practicable, and no later than 5 business days, after making a decision to which this
-- section applies, the health ombudsman must give notice to the complainant ...".
-- Time is counted in calendar days from the start of the period; the deadline is the end of the last business day.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the business days for the decision` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice must also be within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Ombudsman party` `Ombudsman act`
`decide and then tell the complainant` `the start` `the public holidays` `the business days for the decision` `the notice must also be within the period` MEANS
    PARTY `the health ombudsman`
    MUST `decide on day` `the day decided`
    WITHIN `the number of days from` `the start` `until` (`the business day after` `the business days for the decision` `the start` `the public holidays`)
    HENCE
        PARTY `the health ombudsman`
        MUST `give the complainant notice of the decision`
        WITHIN `the notice days allowed` `the start` `the public holidays` `the business days for the decision` `the notice must also be within the period` `the day decided`
        LEST BREACH BY `the health ombudsman` BECAUSE "the complainant was not given notice of the decision in time (s 278(1), and s 35(1)(b) where it applies)"
    LEST BREACH BY `the health ombudsman` BECAUSE "the decision was not made within the period the Act allows (s 35(1) or s 49(1))"

-- s 278(1) alone: notice within 5 business days after a decision (time counted in calendar days from the decision).
GIVEN `the decision day` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Ombudsman party` `Ombudsman act`
`tell the complainant of the decision` `the decision day` `the public holidays` MEANS
    PARTY `the health ombudsman`
    MUST `give the complainant notice of the decision`
    WITHIN `the number of days from` `the decision day` `until` (`the business day after` 5 `the decision day` `the public holidays`)
    LEST BREACH BY `the health ombudsman` BECAUSE "the complainant was not given notice of the decision within 5 business days (s 278(1))"

-- A trace that ends FULFILLED. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. These
-- take a DEONTIC value, so they are never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Ombudsman party` `Ombudsman act`
      `the decision offset days` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice offset days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision and notice are in time under` `the rule` `the decision offset days` `the notice offset days` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the decision offset days`), (EVENT `the health ombudsman` (`decide on day` `the decision offset days`) `the decision offset days`), (WAITUNTIL `the notice offset days`), (EVENT `the health ombudsman` `give the complainant notice of the decision` `the notice offset days`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Ombudsman party` `Ombudsman act`
      `the notice offset days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is in time under` `the rule` `the notice offset days` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the notice offset days`), (EVENT `the health ombudsman` `give the complainant notice of the decision` `the notice offset days`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The states of a decide-then-tell duty, as the complainant sees them.
DECLARE `Decision and notice state` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the decision was made, and I was told of it, within the periods the Act allows`
    `the decision was made in time, but I was told of it after the period the Act allows had ended`
    `the decision was made after the period the Act allows had ended`
    `the decision was made in time; I have not been told yet, but the period for telling me has not ended`
    `the decision was made in time, but the period for telling me has ended and I have not been told`
    `not yet due: no decision yet, but the period for it has not ended`
    `overdue: the period for the decision has ended and no decision has been made`

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the business days for the decision` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice must also be within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was decided` IS A DATE
      `I have been told` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was told` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Decision and notice state`
`the state of the decision and notice` `the start` `the public holidays` `the business days for the decision` `the notice must also be within the period` `it has been decided` `the day it was decided` `I have been told` `the day I was told` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been decided`
    THEN IF (NOT (`the day it was decided` `is on or before` `the last day for the decision`))
         THEN `the decision was made after the period the Act allows had ended`
         ELSE IF `I have been told`
              THEN IF `the decision and notice are in time under` `the rule` (`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the day it was decided`) (`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the day I was told`)
                   THEN `yes: the decision was made, and I was told of it, within the periods the Act allows`
                   ELSE `the decision was made in time, but I was told of it after the period the Act allows had ended`
              ELSE IF `today` `is on or before` `the last day to tell me`
                   THEN `the decision was made in time; I have not been told yet, but the period for telling me has not ended`
                   ELSE `the decision was made in time, but the period for telling me has ended and I have not been told`
    ELSE IF `today` `is on or before` `the last day for the decision`
         THEN `not yet due: no decision yet, but the period for it has not ended`
         ELSE `overdue: the period for the decision has ended and no decision has been made`
    WHERE
        `the rule` MEANS `decide and then tell the complainant` `the start` `the public holidays` `the business days for the decision` `the notice must also be within the period`
        `the last day for the decision` MEANS `the business day after` `the business days for the decision` `the start` `the public holidays`
        `the decision offset` MEANS `the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the day it was decided`
        `the notice allowance` MEANS `the notice days allowed` `the start` `the public holidays` `the business days for the decision` `the notice must also be within the period` `the decision offset`
        `the last day to tell me` MEANS (`the decision offset` PLUS `the notice allowance`) `days after` `the start`
